1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gards- og ættesoge for Sveio I page 144 Ulvaråker (38h).
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Stord pr.gj. 1848 No. 98: https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/8303/60
2 CONT
2 CONT To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/149994262/andrew-brown
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Brown died at the hospital at Whitehall on May 10, 1921, at the age of 72 years, 8 months and 10 days after an illness of only four days of blood poisoning. The funeral services were held from the U.N. Lutheran church in Bl
2 CONC air on Friday afternoon May 20, Rev. Boe officiating. Mr. Brown was born at Ulveraaker, Norway, on August 9, 1849. He was the son of Reier and Louise B. Brown. He came to America, in 1867, first locating at Black River Falls. In 1
2 CONC 870 he moved to a farm about three miles south of Taylor. He was successfully engaged in farming there until 1918, when he purchased a home and moved to Black River Falls.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married on May 1881, to Miss Inga Olson, who now survives him, with four sons and five daughters, as follows:
2 CONT 1. Mrs. Louise Hjerleid of Taylor;
2 CONT 2. Levi Brown of Blair;
2 CONT 3. Mrs. Sadie Brown of Wichita Falls, Texas; 4. Mrs. Rose Ellison of Blair; 5. Arthur Brown of Mabel, Minnesota; 6. Miss Inez Brown of Black River Falls, 7. Arthur Brown of Mabel, Minn.; 8. Tennie Brown of Taylor; 9. Octavia Brown
2 CONC  of Mabel, Minn.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also leaves one sister residing at Taylor and one at Devils Lake, N.D.; two sisters in Norway and one brother. He is also survived by 13 grandchildren. Mr. Brown has been a member of the Lutheran church since boyhood. He was an
2 CONC  honest and industrious man, and he developed a good farming property on the place on which he made his home for nearly a half century. He was devoted to his family and in the community in which he made his home so many years. He 
2 CONC was favorably regarded by a large circle of friends. His many friends extend their sympathy and sorrow to his bereaved family and relatives in their sorrow. All of the children were present at the funeral, excepting Bennie Brown o
2 CONC f Wichita Falls, Texas.
2 CONT
2 CONT THE BLAIR PRESS - MAY 25, 1921
2 CONT
2 CONT (Obituary provided by FAG contributor Cyndi Berg Jearman)
