2 CONT [https://media.digitalarkivet.no/kb20070222690245 '''Fødsel og dåp:''']
2 CONT
2 CONT USA 20/5.1869
2 CONT
2 CONT Lived 1900 in Springfield, Jackson, Wisconsin
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Serena Jermstad died at the home of Ingval Hegg, January 16, 1939 at 11 a.m. at the age of 91 years and five months. Mrs. Jermstad had been bedridden for the past seven years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Norway in August 1847 and came to America and Jackson County in 1867. In 1869, she was united in marriage to Ole P. Jermstad. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Twelve children were born to this union. Mrs. Jermstad’s husband died December 20, 1922 and four children preceded her in death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are the following children: 
2 CONT 1. Helen, Mrs. Ingval Hegg, Taylor; 
2 CONT 2. Mrs. Pete (Anna) Moe, Black River Falls; 
2 CONT 3. Mrs. Ida Tormoen, Minneapolis, Minnesota; 
2 CONT 4. Sadie, Mrs. Clinton C. Veeder, Watertown, South Dakota; 
2 CONT 5. Sam and 
2 CONT 6. Bennie, Taylor; 
2 CONT 7. Peter Olaus of LaCrosse and 
2 CONT 8. Olaf/Ole P Jr., of Fargo, North Dakota. 
2 CONT Deceased were:
2 CONT 9. Bertha Louise (Louis J) Oakland (1874-1934) of Superior, WI
2 CONT 10. Kjerstina (Iver Cornel) Olson of Ettrick died in 1913
2 CONT
