1 NAME Octave Sedolph Lloyd /Brown/
2 GIVN Octave Sedolph Lloyd
2 SURN Brown
2 _MARNM Brown
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 14 FEB 1903
2 ADDR
3 CITY Springfield
3 STAE Wisconsin
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 JUN 1949
2 ADDR
3 CITY Independence
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/13871278/octave-sedolph_lloyd-brown
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Andrew Brown and Inga Olson.
2 CONT At the age of 18 he moved to Mabel, Minnesota.
2 CONT After his marriage he farmed near Caledonia, Minnesota for seven years and then to Mabel, Minnesota where he farmed for three years.
2 CONT In 1940 he moved to Canton, Minnesota whee he became identified with nursery interests.
2 CONT The Brown family moved to Postville in 1944 and started the Northeast Iowa Nursery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and Emma were the parents of five daughters: Virginia, Lorraine, Beverly, Janice, and Sharon.
2 CONT ∼
2 CONT Postville Herald, Postville, Iowa, Wednesday, June 8, 1949.
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONC ----------.
2 CONT
2 CONT Final Rites Are Held On Monday For O. L. Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held Monday morning at 10:00 o'clock for O. L. Brown, 46, at St. Paul's Lutheran church with Rev. F. B. Ludwig officiating. Burial was in Blair, Wisconsin, where services were conducted by Rev. Ludwig and Rev
2 CONC . Lawrence Halvorson, pastor of Zion Lutheran church of Blair.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Brown, who had been established in the nursery business in Postville since 1944, passed away Thursday, June 2, following a lengthy illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born In Wisconsin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Octave Sedolph Lloyed Brown, son of Andrew Brown and Inga Olson Brown, was born February 14, 1903, at Springfield, Jackson county, Wisconsin, and departed this life June 2, 1949, at Independence, aged 46 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Brown was united in marriage with Emma Bjergum of Black Hammer, Minnesota, at Riceford, Minnesota, on November 21, 1927. To this union five children were born, all of whom survive the passing of their father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Brown spent the earlier years of his life at Taylor, Wisconsin. At the age of 18 he removed to Mabel, Minnesota. After his marriage the family home was established at Caledonia, Minnesota, where he engaged in farming for seven
2 CONC  years. The family home was then removed to Mabel, where he farmed for three years. In November 1940 the family moved to Canton, Minnesota, where Mr. Brown became identified with nursery interests. On March 1, 1944, the family est
2 CONC ablished their home in Postville where Mr. Brown set himself to the task of building up a nursery of his own, meanwhile continuing as representative of an already established nursery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Brown is survived by his widow; five children:
2 CONT 1. Virginia,
2 CONT 2. Lorraine (Mrs. Cloy Schultz, Jr.),
2 CONT 3. Beverly,
2 CONT 4. Janice and
2 CONT 5. Sharon Kay, all of Postville;
2 CONT six brothers and sisters: Levi Brown, Blair, Wisconsin; Sadie (Mrs. Ludvig Hjerleid), Blair, Wisconsin; Rose (Mrs. John Ellison), Blair, Wisconsin; Arthur Brown, Spring Grove, Minnesota; Tennis Brown, Green, North Dakota, and Inez
2 CONC  (Mrs. Joseph Manford Johnson), Black River Falls, Wisconsin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Brown was preceded in death by his parents; one sister, Louise (Mrs. Octave Hjerleid), and one brother Bennie Brown.
