1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1880 census family had "Peterson" as last name
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole Peterson Jermstad, another old, respected pioneer of this section passed away at his home in Skutley Coulee, Friday, December 29, 1922 at the ripe old age of 85 years, 8 months and 23 days. Mr. Jermstad suffered a stroke of pa
2 CONC ralysis five days previous and this was the immediate cause of his death. He also suffered a stroke about five years ago but recovered except for his speech which was slightly impaired. His health had been fairly good, considering
2 CONC  his advanced age, even the last few years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased was born in Trondhjem, Verdalen, Norway, April 6, 1837 and came to this county, arriving in LaCrosse in 1867. He later moved to Black River Falls where he was employed by A.J. Spaulding in the then thriving lumber industr
2 CONC y. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Miss Serena Brown and in 1869 and in 1874 moved to the Town of Springfield and settled in Skutley Coulee. He was the second to settle in upper Skutley Coulee, and has seen this entire section develop from a wilderness t
2 CONC o its present high state of development. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Twelve children were born to this union.  four children preceded his wife in death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving him are the following children: 
2 CONT 1. Helen, Mrs. Ingval Hegg, (1885-1967) of Taylor, WI
2 CONT 2. Bertha Louise (Louis J) Oakland (1874-1934) of Superior 
2 CONT 3. Mrs. Pete L (Anna P) Moe, (1872-1955) of Black River Falls; 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Mrs. Ida Tormon-Horn, (1890-1975) of Minneapolis, MN
2 CONT Married George N Tormon and later Julius Horn; note: George Tormon’s parents were Tormoen
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Sadie, Mrs. Clinton C. Veeder (1893-1981) of Watertown, South Dakota; 
2 CONT 6. Sam (married Mathilda Pederson) and 
2 CONT 7. Bernhardt/Bennie, Taylor; 
2 CONT 8. Peter Olaus Jermstad (1880-1971) of LaCrosse and 
2 CONT 9. Ole P (1882-1962) of Fargo, North Dakota. 
2 CONT 10. Kjerstina (Iver Cornel) Olson of Ettrick died in 1913
2 CONT
2 CONT Reprinted from the Taylor Herald THE BLAIR PRESS - JANUARY 18, 1923* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/179144149/ole-peterson-jermstad Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy
