2 CONT
2 CONT To America 1857.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/144890136/reier-torbjornsen-thompson
2 CONT
2 CONT Reier Torbjornsen Thompson BIRTH	17 Sep 1844 Valestrand, Osterøy kommune (Wrong, Sveio kommune), Hordaland fylke, Norway DEATH	10 Aug 1927 (aged 82) Long Beach, Los Angeles County, California, USA BURIAL	 Beach Lutheran Cemetery B
2 CONC each, Golden Valley County, North Dakota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial unknown, but I suspect same cemetery as his wife. Hope to find out.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reir Thompson was born in Norway Arrived in US about 1857 By 1860 he was living in Springfield, Jackson County, WI He married Bromhilde S Haugland in 1864 in neighboring Trempealeau County. They continued to live in Springfield th
2 CONC rough at least 1880 census.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1900 and 1905 lived in BLAIR, Trempealeau County, WI In 1910 lived in Beach, ND In 1920 he was living in Long Beach, CA with widowed daughter Thea Anderson and also near daughter Alice Knutson.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had at least the following childen (could be more) 1. Charles 1865-1949 of Grafton ND 2. Thea Serena (Andrew) Anderson 1866-1940 in Long Beach 3. Julia Caroline (Peter A) Larson (1870-1896) of Grafton, ND died several years a
2 CONC go, her son was Randall Bertram Larson born 1893, lived with grandparents 1900 in Blair 4. Nels A Thompson 1871-1942 of BLAIR, Wisconsin 5. Henry R Thompson of Beach d 1959 married Ida Amela Tenneson of Blair, WI 6. Alice Burnhild
2 CONC e (Julius O) Knutson of Long Beach, CA 7. Thomas Thompson died at age 3 near BLAIR, WI 8. Albert R Thompson died in 1933 in Beach, ND, he married Victoria Serine Thompson of Hixton. Her brother Erick J Thompson moved to Long Beach
2 CONC , CA 9. Isabella Josephine died in Beach, ND in 1911 10. Rudolph Benjamin died in 1911 in Beach ND
2 CONT
2 CONT ***********************************
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1914 article about 50th anniversary
2 CONT
2 CONT In their ffifty years of wedded life, Mr. and Mrs. Thompson became the happy parents of six boys and four girls. A boy and girl, 1. Thomas and 2. Isabelle, died in childhood, while another daughter, 3. Julia, died after she was ma
2 CONC rried twenty years ago. (Abt 1894)
2 CONT
2 CONT All of the remaining children are happily married and were here for the reunion and the golden wedding celebration. They are 4. Charles L. Thompson of Grafton 5. Nels Thompson of Taylor, Wis., 6. Mrs. Julius O. (Alice) Knutson (Lo
2 CONC ng Beach, CA) 7. Mrs. Andrew (Thea) Anderson of Blair, Wis., 8-10. Albert, Rudolph and Henry of Beach
2 CONT
2 CONT ******************************************* From Nels obituary in 1942: family of ten, two brothers and a sister survive: 7. Charles, Grafton, N. D.,1865-1949 8. Henry, Beach, N. D., (died 1959) 9. Alice (Mrs. J. O. Knutson), Long
2 CONC  Beach,Calif.
2 CONT
2 CONT His mother passed away at Beach, N. D. June 30, 1916 and his father at Long Beach, Calif. on 10 August 1927.
2 CONT
2 CONT Six brothers and sisters preceded him in death: 1. Thomas at the age of 3 years, 2. Rudolph Nov. 11, 1918, 3. Albert at Beach N.D. in 1933, 4. Julia (Mrs. Peter Larson) several years ago, (about 1894) 5. Isabel at Beach, N. D. in 
2 CONC 1912 and 6. Thea Serena (Mrs. Andrew Anderson) at Long Beach, Calif. Dec. 9, 1940. (note: His father living with her, a widow.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ******************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother Thom Thompson is buried in Curran Valley, Jackson County, WI
