2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/151643984/thomas-thompson
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas “Tom” Thompson BIRTH	10 Aug 1848 Norway DEATH	8 Aug 1924 (aged 75) Eleva, Trempealeau County, Wisconsin, USA BURIAL	 Curran Valley Cemetery Taylor, Jackson County, Wisconsin, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Tjerand Tjorbjornson Thompson and Gunvor Reiersdtr Ulveraker The father died in 1893 in Jackson County, WI
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: Ingeborg, Reier, Serena and Ed
2 CONT
2 CONT His obituary incorrectly lists his daughter Mabel Thompson (Mrs Peter M) Gilberg as his sister. It later identifies her as a child.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thom Thompson an old pioneer of Curran died at the home of his daughter Mrs PM Gilberg in Eleva on August 8, 1924.
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to US with parents 1857 first to Dane County and a few years later to Curran Valley.
2 CONT
2 CONT His children: 1. Mrs Isabelle (Nels S) Fagerlund (Mondovi) 2. Mrs Mabel (Peter M) Gilberg of Eleva 3. Theodore Thompson of Eleva and Jackson Co., and 4. Clarence (of Minneapolis) were at his bedside when he passed. 5. Mrs Thea "Ju
2 CONC lia" (SA) Bue and 6. Andrew M Thompson both of Hixton who were with him while he was ill.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services were held at Curran Valley Lutheran church (Rev Wichman of Eleva and Rev Lovaas of Taylor officiating) with interment in the Curran Valley cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT First married in 1869 to Malinda Halvorson Two Children: Thea Julia Bue (Survives) and Tjarand Syvert deceased in infancy in 1872 the same year as Wife Malinda
2 CONT
2 CONT Married again to Martha Anderson and nine children born to them, three dying in infancy. A daughter Serena died in 1902. His wife Martha passed away in 1910 (grave stone has date)
2 CONT
2 CONT A brother Reier of Long Beach and a sister Serena, Mrs Knut Skutley A brother Ed/Oliver died 1923 in canwood, Sask, Canada and sister Ingeborg/Isabele Nelson of Jackson County died in 1908
2 CONT
