2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/162818229/serine-skutley
2 CONT
2 CONT Serine Thompson Skutley BIRTH	14 Oct 1850 Norway DEATH	14 Dec 1925 (aged 75) Hixton, Jackson County, Wisconsin, USA BURIAL	 Curran Valley Cemetery Taylor, Jackson County, Wisconsin, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Tjerand Thorbjornson and Gunvor Reirsdtr Ulvaker Thompson
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Thom Thompson (buried Curran Valley) and Reier Thompson of Beach, ND and Long Beach, CA
2 CONT
2 CONT Serine Thompson was born in Norway on October 14, 1850. When she was four years of age, her parents came to America with their family and settled in Trump Coulee in the Town of Springfield, where they made their home.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was united in marriage with Knudt Iverson Skutley on April 14, 1870. To this union were born eleven children. Most of their married life was spent on a farm in the Town of Curran. Her husband preceded her in death ten years ag
2 CONC o. Her last illness was of short duration and all that loving hand could do was done to care for her.
2 CONT
2 CONT She passed away at her home in Hixton, December 14, 1925, at the age of 75 years and two months.
2 CONT
2 CONT She is survived by eight children, six sons and two daughters: 1. Nels, 2. Theodore, 3. Andrew and 4. Evert of Sechlerville; 5. Sedolph of York; (1894-1987) 6. Helmer of Minneapolis; 7. Ellen (Mrs. Frank Nesuen) and 8. Isabella (M
2 CONC rs. Fred Olson) both of Minneapolis. 9. Louis K Skutley (1889-1924) married Tilda Lund, son Truman Also one brother, Rier Thompson of Long Beach, California.
2 CONT
