1 NAME Emma /Bjergum/
2 GIVN Emma
2 SURN Bjergum
2 _MARNM Brown
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 17 DEC 1905
2 PLAC Black Hammer twp., Spring Grove, MN
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 27 FEB 1986
2 PLAC North Gate Care Center, Waukon, IA, buried in Postville cemetery.
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/13871272/emma-brown
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Jens Bjergum and Martha Omodt, born in Black Hammer, Minnesota.
2 CONT Wife of Octave Brown, married 27 Nov 1927 at Black Hammer.
2 CONT They were the parents of five daughters.
2 CONT They farmed until 1939 and then started a nursery business in Minnesota.
2 CONT In 1944 they came to Iowa and started the Northeast Iowa Nursery.
2 CONT She continued to run the nursery a few years after her husband's death in 1949.
1 FAMS @F6000000003889527664@
1 RFN geni:6000000003888884494
1 SUBM @S6000000003887373302@
1 NOTE Funeral services were held Monday March 3, 1986 at St. Paul's Lutheran church in Postville.  The Rev. Julius L. Peterson officiated.  She attended rural school in Black Hammer and the Spring Grove high school. She was employed in 
2 CONC the Spring Grove telephone office years ago.  Her and Octave farmed in the Mabel area until 1939 when they started a nursery business.  Feb 1944 the family moved to Postville, IA and started the Northeran Iowa Nursery.  After her 
2 CONC husban died she continued the nursery business for a number of years.  She was a member of St. Paul Lutheran church, Luther Church Women and the Republican Women's Club.   Survived by 11 grandchildren, 9 great-grandchildren .  Her
2 CONC  husband, four brothers and three sisters have died.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 28 JAN 2023
3 TIME 13:47:33
