3 CITY Skjold
3 STAE Rogaland
3 CTRY Norway
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 OCT 1950
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cedar Rapids
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tysvær Gard og ætt 5 page 92 Fikstveit (20f).
2 CONT
2 CONT To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/141459669/jacob-severin-jacobson
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob S. Jacobson, 76, a resident of Cedar Rapids, IA for 25 years, died at his home Saturday afternoon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born August 16, 1874, in Norway, Europe, he married Inger Kolsto November 19, 1900. He farmed near Norway, IA before moving to Cedar Rapids in 1925.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are two sons, Sewall, of Baltimore, MD, and Gerald, of Philadelphia, PA; and five daughters, Margaret, at home, Mrs. Ida Day, Mrs. Lillian Bell, Mrs. Clara Blessing, and Mrs. Alta Stevens, all of Cedar Rapids.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceding him in death are his wife, who died four years ago, and one son, Merrill, born in January of 1903 in Iowa and died on May 27, 1903. He is buried in Norway, Europe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services: 2:00 p.m. Monday at the Chapel of Memories in Cedar Memorial cemetery by the Rev. H. G. Schwegler, pastor of First Lutheran church. Visitation will be at the Janeba funeral home after 4:00 p.m. Sunday.
2 CONT Burial: Cedar Memorial cemetery.
