1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Torborg was raised by an aunt who had two daughters and she served as a housemaid to her aunt.  She just attended school for a few years.
2 CONT
2 CONT One day one of the daughters brought a young Captain of a Sea Vessel home to meet the family.  He fell in love with Torborg and they were married.  Two years later Ingebord was born on June 16, 1875 Thomas was born on May 27, 1878
2 CONC .  Early in 1881 or 1882 he came home from voyage very ill in within a few days he died.  They called the disease consumption but it probably was pneumonia.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death, Torborg resolved that her son should not be a seaman and much against her father's wishes, she packed up her two children and came to America.  She arrived in the United States on May 10, 1882.  She traveled to a 
2 CONC Norweigian settlement near Story City, Iowa.  Soon after arriving both children became seriously ill with a fever.  Ingebord died and was buried in Iowa but Thomas survived.
2 CONT
2 CONT Torborg married Thomas L. Thompson in 1882 in Story City, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha, Lewis, and Ole were born in Iowa, Arthur, Benjamin, Thea, Anna, Jenetta and Ethel were all born in Wyoming.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some of the family history indicates that she was called Thea.  On of their daughters was named Thea as well.
2 CONT
2 CONT Torborg died in Lusk, Wyoming.  Her death certificate indicates that the cause of death was cirrhosis of the liver.  She is buried in the Thompson family plot in Plesant View Cemetary near the community of Kirtley, Wyoming.
