1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/80088975/willard-august_eldo-sander
2 CONT
2 CONT Willard August Eldo Sander, son of Walter Fred and Amanda E. (Schutte) Sander, was born September 17, 1926 in Post Township, Allamakee County, near Postville, Iowa. He was baptized December 18, 1926 by the Rev. E. T. Finck at St. 
2 CONC Paul Lutheran Church in Postville and confirmed there on March 17, 1940 by the Rev. Frederick R. Ludwig. Willard graduated from the Luana High School and then began farming with his parents on the family farm.
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 30, 1952 Willard was married to Beverly Ann Brown. They had three children. This marriage apparently ended in divorce. Their son, Dan, farmed with him from 1980 until 1987, when Willard retired. He moved to Luana short
2 CONC ly before his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Luana, Iowa on November 21, 1992. Funeral services were held Wednesday, November 25, 1992 St. Paul Lutheran Church, Postville, Iowa. Burial was in the Postville Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents. Survivors were a son, Lynn of Robinsdale, MN, a daughter, Marcee Sander of Golden Valley, MN, and a son, Danny and his wife, Lynette and their son, Clinton of McGregor, Iowa; a brother Wayn
2 CONC e Sander and his wife, Jean, of New Hampton, IA, and a sister, Irene and her husband, Leonard Wiedenman of Cedar Rapids, Iowa.
