1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/141459781/inger-agnette-jacobson
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Inger Jacobson, 72, of Cedar Rapids, IA, died Friday following an illness of several weeks.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born July 18, 1874, in Kopervik, Norway, she came to the U.S. at the age of 13. She was married to Jacob Jacobson November 19, 1900, and they lived on a farm northeast of Norway for many years before moving to Cedar Rapids in 1925
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving besides her husband are two sons, Sewall and Jerry of Philadelphia, PA; five daughters, Margaret at home, Mrs. Ida Day, Mrs. Lillian Bell, Mrs. Clara Blessing, and Mrs. Alta Stevens; two brothers, Swen Kolsto of Cedar Ra
2 CONC pids, Knute Kolsto of Atkins, IA; a sister, Andrea Lande of Norway; and six grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Preceding Inger in death are her parents, Lars and Marta Kolsto; one son, Merrill, born in January of 1903 in Iowa and died on May 27, 1903. He is buried in Norway, Europe; two brothers, Iver and Lars.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services: 2:00 p.m. Monday in Cedar Memorial chapel. Visitation will be Saturday evening an Sunday at the Janeba-Trachta funeral home.
2 CONT Burial: Cedar Memorial cemetery.
