1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/107070089/magnus-miller
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus Miller BIRTH	25 Oct 1888 Vester Hassing, Alborg Kommune, Nordjylland, Denmark DEATH	14 Sep 1959 (aged 70) BURIAL	 Story City Cemetery Story City, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Hans Miller and Annie Marie Hanson.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Nevada Journal September 29, 1959 (page 4)
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Services Held For Magnus Miller
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Services for Magnus Miller were held Thursday afternoon, Sept. 18, at 1:30 in the Larson Funeral Home and 2:00 in Bethel Lutheran Church, Story City with interment in the Story City Municipal cemetery. The Rev. A. J. Bring
2 CONC le officiated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Luther Matson and Mrs. Homer Olson sang at the church service, with Mrs. Bert Stensland at the organ.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pall bearers were Irvin Lund, Lars Kalvik, Lars Raymond, Andrew Enderson, Arthur Goodmanson and Hans Hendrickson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT Magnus Miller was the third child born to Anna Marie and Hans Nelson Miller. He was born October 25, 1888 at Gammil Stendrup, Vester Hasinge, Denmark and died Sept. 14, 1959 at the age of 70 years, 11 months and 19 days. He was ba
2 CONC ptized on December 16 1888 in Sandhard Lyndise Church and confirmed October 1902 in the Lutheran Faith.
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to this country at the age of sixteen and settled in this community, where he has resided most of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was united in marriage to Ellen Wike on Feb. 12, 1914 at the Elim Lutheran Church at Randall, Ia. To this unions six children were born. They are: Clarence and Clifton of Story City; Arnold of Stanhope; Franklin of Seattle, Was
2 CONC h.; Arlene (Mrs. Edward Wirth) of Story City and Ruth (Mrs. Wesley Warren) of Ames.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by his wife and six children, also 25 grandchildren, one brother, Emil of Los Angeles, Calif. and four brothers and three sisters in Denmark.
2 CONT
